Z||000005||Monkeyman||11-30-1999||01:19 PM||||Are we sure that it's really a GT, not an'86 SE with GT sailpanels?  I thought all GTs' had wings and that the luggage rack wasn't even an option for them.  I'm probably wrong, but just an observation.  Also, what's up with the lower door moulding?  It looks like it's too short.  Or did they do that to jack up the car?||||reg||5
Z||000006||fiero56||11-30-1999||03:44 PM||||There were no notchback GTs for the '86 model year. The "and a half" just means the design came out half way through the year.  Luggage racks were available on the 86GTs, and spoilers were standard equipment only on the Indy and Formula models.  Spoilers were optional on all GT Fieros.<BR>The '85 GT is the only GT to have those wheels in the picture, all the other GTs had diamond spoke. <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-30-1999).]||||reg||1
